{"id": "RT-science-genetics-gen-12", "body": {"t": "main", "a": {"class": "wrap", "id": "main-content"}, "c": [" ", " ", {"t": "p", "a": {"class": "kicker"}, "c": ["Confirmed science / Genetics · GEN-12"]}, " ", {"t": "h1", "c": ["The 27 ADHD risk loci: a closer look"]}, " ", {"t": "div", "a": {"class": "article-meta"}, "c": [{"t": "span", "a": {"class": "badge"}, "c": ["Last updated 5 October 2026"]}, {"t": "span", "a": {"class": "badge"}, "c": ["GEN-12"]}]}, " ", {"t": "details", "a": {"class": "toc", "open": "true"}, "c": [{"t": "summary", "c": ["On this page"]}, {"t": "ol", "c": [{"t": "li", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#what-the-27-loci-represent"}, "c": ["What the 27 loci represent"]}]}, {"t": "li", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#how-to-use-the-locus-links"}, "c": ["How to use the locus links"]}]}, {"t": "li", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#locus-index"}, "c": ["Locus index"]}]}, {"t": "li", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#the-27-regions-in-detail"}, "c": ["The 27 regions in detail"]}]}, {"t": "li", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#what-needs-distinguishing"}, "c": ["What needs distinguishing"]}]}, {"t": "li", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#the-deeper-layer-optional-to-read"}, "c": ["The deeper layer (optional to read)"]}]}, {"t": "li", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#what-this-evidence-can-tell-us"}, "c": ["What this evidence can tell us"]}]}, {"t": "li", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#sources"}, "c": ["Sources"]}]}]}]}, " ", {"t": "div", "a": {"class": "article-body gen-article"}, "c": [" ", {"t": "h2", "a": {"id": "what-the-27-loci-represent"}, "c": ["What the 27 loci represent"]}, " ", {"t": "p", "c": ["Demontis and colleagues reported 27 genome-wide significant ADHD risk regions in a 2023 analysis of 38,691 cases and 186,843 controls. Each row below is a region anchored by an index variant, not a confirmed causal gene or a diagnostic result. The paper reports 32 independent lead variants across these 27 regions; this guide follows its Table 1, one entry per region ", {"t": "sup", "a": {"class": "cite"}, "c": ["[", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#src-1", "aria-label": "Source 1"}, "c": ["1"]}, "]"]}, "."]}, " ", {"t": "p", "c": ["A different 2025 analysis incorporating childhood symptom scores reported 39 ", {"t": "a", "a": {"class": "gloss", "href": "/science/genetics/gen-11/#g-locus", "title": "A region of DNA"}, "c": ["loci"]}, " under its own study design. The counts should not be added together or read as a simple time series. See ", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "/science/genetics/gen-01/"}, "c": ["GEN-01"]}, " for the broader context ", {"t": "sup", "a": {"class": "cite"}, "c": ["[", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#src-2", "aria-label": "Source 2"}, "c": ["2"]}, "]"]}, "."]}, " ", {"t": "h2", "a": {"id": "how-to-use-the-locus-links"}, "c": ["How to use the locus links"]}, " ", {"t": "p", "c": ["Select a locus in the index to jump to its entry. Chromosome positions use the paper’s hg19 reference assembly. The listed genes are within 50 kb of the index variant in Table 1; an empty cell means that table listed none in that window. The odds ratio is for effect allele A1, comparing alleles in this study, and is not an individual prediction. P values describe association evidence, not the size or clinical meaning of an effect ", {"t": "sup", "a": {"class": "cite"}, "c": ["[", {"t": "a", "a": {"href": "#src-1", "aria-label": "Source 1"}, "c": ["1"]}, "]"]}, "."]}, " ", {"t": "h2", "a": {"id": "locus-index"}, "c": ["Locus index"]}, " ", {"t": "div", "a": {"class": "table-wrap", "role": "region", "aria-label": "Table"}, "c": [{"t": "table", "c": [{"t": "thead", "c": [{"t": "tr", "c": [{"t": "th", "a": {"scope": "col"}, "c": ["Locus"]}, {"t": "th", "a": {"scope": "col"}, "c": ["Index variant"]}, {"t": "th", "a": {"scope": "col"}, "c": ["Chromosome and hg19 position"]}, {"t": "th", "a": {"scope": "col"}, "c": ["Nearby genes within 50 kb"]}]}]}, {"t": "tbody", "c": [{"t": "tr", "c": [{"t": "td", "c": [{"t": "a", "a": {"href